# CKA Drill: Manual Kubeadm Cluster Upgrade (`upgrade`)

Hands-on rehearsal of the manual Kubernetes node and cluster upgrade sequence using `kubeadm`, `kubelet`, and `kubectl`.

## Exam Importance & Constraints

- **Exam Domain**: Cluster Architecture, Installation & Configuration (25%).
- **Frequency**: Present in nearly every CKA exam session.
- **Rules of Thumb**:
  - Always upgrade the control plane node before any worker nodes.
  - Never skip minor versions (e.g. 1.33 $\to$ 1.34 $\to$ 1.35; never 1.33 $\to$ 1.35 directly).
  - Version skew: `kubelet` must never be newer than `kube-apiserver`, and can be at most 1 minor version older.
  - Always `drain` before upgrading `kubelet` on worker nodes; unhold packages before running `apt-get install`.

---

## 1. Control Plane Node Upgrade Procedure

### Step 1: Drain the Control Plane Node (if scheduling application pods)

```bash
kubectl drain <control-plane-node> --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
```

### Step 2: Upgrade kubeadm

```bash
sudo apt-mark unhold kubeadm
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.34.x-1.1
sudo apt-mark hold kubeadm
```

### Step 3: Run Upgrade Plan and Apply

```bash
sudo kubeadm upgrade plan
sudo kubeadm upgrade apply v1.34.x
```

### Step 4: Upgrade kubelet and kubectl

```bash
sudo apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
sudo apt-get install -y kubelet=1.34.x-1.1 kubectl=1.34.x-1.1
sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl
```

### Step 5: Reload and Restart kubelet

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart kubelet
```

### Step 6: Uncordon the Control Plane Node

```bash
kubectl uncordon <control-plane-node>
```

---

## 2. Worker Node Upgrade Procedure

### Step 1: Drain Worker Node (from Control Plane)

```bash
kubectl drain <worker-node> --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
```

### Step 2: SSH into Worker Node & Upgrade kubeadm

```bash
ssh <worker-node>
sudo apt-mark unhold kubeadm
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.34.x-1.1
sudo apt-mark hold kubeadm
```

### Step 3: Upgrade Kubelet Configuration

```bash
sudo kubeadm upgrade node
```

### Step 4: Upgrade kubelet and kubectl Packages

```bash
sudo apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
sudo apt-get install -y kubelet=1.34.x-1.1 kubectl=1.34.x-1.1
sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart kubelet
exit
```

### Step 5: Uncordon Worker Node (from Control Plane)

```bash
kubectl uncordon <worker-node>
kubectl get nodes
```

